{"title": "Sectional Mock #120 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>In &#8710; ABC, &#8736; B and &#8736; C are complementary. And &#8736;B - &#8736;C =20&deg;. AD&#8869;BC at D and the bisector of &#8736;A meets BC at E. If the measure of &#8736;DAE = x&deg;, then find the supplementary angle of x.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#8710;ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;B &#2324;&#2352; &#8736; C &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;B - &#8736;C = 20&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; AD&#8869;BC, D &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;A &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; BC &#2325;&#2379; E &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;DAE &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; = x&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["150&deg;", "140&deg;", "160&deg;", "170&deg;"], "options_hi": ["150&deg;", "140&deg;", "160&deg;", "170&deg;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=419 height=215 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14006/image008.jpg\" alt=O78.JPG></p><p>Given that,</p><p>&#8736; B and &#8736; C are complementary. So,</p><p>&#8736; B + &#8736; C = 90&deg;... (1)</p><p>And given,</p><p>&#8736;B - &#8736;C =20 &deg;.... (2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2),</p><p>We get &#8736; B = 55&deg; and &#8736; C = 35&deg;</p><p>Now, x = (&#8736; B - &#8736; C)/2</p><p>x = (55 - 35)/2</p><p>x = 10</p><p>Supplementary angle of x = 180 - 10 = 170&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=419 height=215 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14006/image008.jpg\" alt=O78.JPG></p><p>Given that,</p><p>&#8736; B and &#8736; C are complementary. So,</p><p>&#8736; B + &#8736; C = 90&deg;... (1)</p><p>And given,</p><p>&#8736;B - &#8736;C =20 &deg;.... (2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2),</p><p>We get &#8736; B = 55&deg; and &#8736; C = 35&deg;</p><p>Now, x = (&#8736; B - &#8736; C)/2</p><p>x = (55 - 35)/2</p><p>x = 10</p><p>Supplementary angle of x = 180 - 10 = 170&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 27662AB is divisible by 80. Then find the value of (A + B) such that B&lt;A&lt;5.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 27662AB, 80 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2379; (A + B) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; B&lt;A&lt;5 &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4", "2", "8", "6"], "options_hi": ["4", "2", "8", "6"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>We know that 80 = 8 x 10 and if a number is divisible by 80, then it must be divisible by 10 and 8.</p><p>For divisible by 10, the last digit of the number should be 0. So, B = 0.</p><p>And for divisible by 8, the last three digits should be divisible by 8.</p><p>The last three digits = 2A0</p><p>To be divisible by 8, the only possible value of A is 4.</p><p>Therefore, (A + B) = 4 + 0 = 4.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that 80 = 8 x 10 and if a number is divisible by 80, then it must be divisible by 10 and 8.</p><p>For divisible by 10, the last digit of the number should be 0. So, B = 0.</p><p>And for divisible by 8, the last three digits should be divisible by 8.</p><p>The last three digits = 2A0</p><p>To be divisible by 8, the only possible value of A is 4.</p><p>Therefore, (A + B) = 4 + 0 = 4.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vendor started selling vegetables at &#8377;10 per kg, but couldn't find buyers at this rate. So he reduced the price to &#8377;7.2 per kg, but uses a faulty weight of 900 g instead of 1 kg. Find the percentage change in the actual price.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2381;&#2332;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; 10 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2311;&#2360; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 7.2 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; 900 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2364;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["10%", "15%", "20%", "25%"], "options_hi": ["10%", "15%", "20%", "25%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>As initially vendor started selling vegetable at 10/kg and then reduced to 7.2/kg for</p><p>900 grams.</p><p>So,</p><p>New price = &#8377;7.2 for 900 g</p><p>So for 1000 grams= (7.2/900)*1000=Rs 8.</p><p>So prcentage change= ((10-8)/10)*100=20%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As initially vendor started selling vegetable at 10/kg and then reduced to 7.2/kg for</p><p>900 grams.</p><p>So,</p><p>New price = &#8377;7.2 for 900 g</p><p>So for 1000 grams= (7.2/900)*1000=Rs 8.</p><p>So prcentage change= ((10-8)/10)*100=20%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two persons Arun and Varun started running around a circular track of length 400 m in opposite directions at speeds of 18 kmph and 27 kmph respectively. After how much time will the two meet for the first time?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; 400 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 27 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["28 sec", "32 sec", "36 sec", "40 sec"], "options_hi": ["28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "32 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed of Varun with respect to Arun = (27+18) = 45 kmph = 45 x 5/18 = 12.5 m/s.</p><p>Therefore time taken for the two to meet for the first time = 400/12.5 = 32 seconds.</p><p>Hence the correct option is (2).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed of Varun with respect to Arun = (27+18) = 45 kmph = 45 x 5/18 = 12.5 m/s.</p><p>Therefore time taken for the two to meet for the first time = 400/12.5 = 32 seconds.</p><p>Hence the correct option is (2).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The graphs of equations x  -  3y = 5 and 2x  -  4y  -  6 = 0 intersect at P(x<sub>1</sub>,y<sub>1</sub>) and graph of x  -  2y + 8 = 0 intersects the y-axis at Q(x<sub>2</sub>,y<sub>2</sub>). Find the value of x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  y<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  y<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; x - 3y = 5 &#2324;&#2352; 2x - 4y - 6 = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; P(x<sub>1</sub>,y<sub>1</sub>) &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; x - 2y + 8 = 0 &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; y-&#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2379; Q(x<sub>2</sub>,y<sub>2</sub>) &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> - y<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> - y<sub>2</sub><sup>2 </sup>&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["-19", "-12", "-10", "-14"], "options_hi": ["-19", "-12", "-10", "-14"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>x  -  3y = 5 .. (1)</p><p>2x  -  4y  -  6 = 0 .. (2)</p><p>If (1) and (2) intersect at P(x<sub>1</sub>,y<sub>1</sub>), then P must satisfy both equations.</p><p>Hence,</p><p>x<sub>1</sub>  -  3y<sub>1</sub> = 5 .. (3)</p><p>2x<sub>1</sub>  -  4y<sub>1</sub>  -  6 = 0 .. (4)</p><p>Solve (3) and (4), we get;</p><p>x<sub>1</sub> = -1 and y<sub>1</sub> = -2</p><p>x  -  2y + 8 = 0 intersect the y-axis at Q(x<sub>2</sub>,y<sub>2</sub>).</p><p>At y-axis x = 0</p><p>Hence, x<sub>2</sub> = 0</p><p>Hence, (0,y<sub>2</sub>) must satisfy the equation x  -  2y = -8.</p><p>0  -  2y<sub>2</sub> = -8</p><p>y<sub>2</sub> = 4</p><p>Therefore, x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  y<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  y<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> = (-1)<sup>2</sup> + (0)<sup>2</sup>  -  (-2)<sup>2</sup>  -  4<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 1 + 0  -  4 - 16</p><p>= -19</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x  -  3y = 5 .. (1)</p><p>2x  -  4y  -  6 = 0 .. (2)</p><p>If (1) and (2) intersect at P(x<sub>1</sub>,y<sub>1</sub>), then P must satisfy both equations.</p><p>Hence,</p><p>x<sub>1</sub>  -  3y<sub>1</sub> = 5 .. (3)</p><p>2x<sub>1</sub>  -  4y<sub>1</sub>  -  6 = 0 .. (4)</p><p>Solve (3) and (4), we get;</p><p>x<sub>1</sub> = -1 and y<sub>1</sub> = -2</p><p>x  -  2y + 8 = 0 intersect the y-axis at Q(x<sub>2</sub>,y<sub>2</sub>).</p><p>At y-axis x = 0</p><p>Hence, x<sub>2</sub> = 0</p><p>Hence, (0,y<sub>2</sub>) must satisfy the equation x  -  2y = -8.</p><p>0  -  2y<sub>2</sub> = -8</p><p>y<sub>2</sub> = 4</p><p>Therefore, x<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + x<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  y<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>  -  y<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> = (-1)<sup>2</sup> + (0)<sup>2</sup>  -  (-2)<sup>2</sup>  -  4<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 1 + 0  -  4 - 16</p><p>= -19</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the area of the base, height, and volume of a right hexagonal prism are (3&radic;3X<sup>2</sup>/2) cm<sup>2</sup>, 20&radic;3 cm, and 70560 cm<sup>3</sup> respectively. then find the value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2359;&#2335;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339;&#2368;&#2351; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;, &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; (3&radic;3X<sup>2</sup>/2) &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>, 20&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 70560 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["28", "24", "26", "30"], "options_hi": ["28", "24", "26", "30"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The volume of a right prism = Area of base * Height</p><p>70560 = (3&radic;3X<sup>2</sup>)/2 * 20&radic;3</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> = 784</p><p>X = 28 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The volume of a right prism = Area of base * Height</p><p>70560 = (3&radic;3X<sup>2</sup>)/2 * 20&radic;3</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> = 784</p><p>X = 28 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Simplify <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;: <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "options_en": ["1", "x + y + z", "2", "1/2"], "options_hi": ["1", "x + y + z", "2", "1/2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=133 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image054.png\"></p><p><img width=207 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image055.png\"></p><p><img width=283 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image056.png\"></p><p><img width=100 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image057.png\"></p><p>= 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=133 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image054.png\"></p><p><img width=207 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image055.png\"></p><p><img width=283 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image056.png\"></p><p><img width=100 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23333/image057.png\"></p><p>= 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vendor at a farmers' market offers a 10% discount on a 10 kg pack of lentils. The cost price for him is &#8377;40 per kg, and the pack is marked at &#8377;50 per kg. However, his weighing scale is rigged- it shows 1 kg when it weighs only 850 grams. What is the vendor's actual profit percentage? (Round off to two decimal places.)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2332;&#2364;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2342;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; 10 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 40 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; 50 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2380;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2376;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2327;&#2337;&#2364;&#2348;&#2337;&#2364; &#2361;&#2376; - &#2351;&#2361; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 850 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;)</p>", "options_en": ["29.11%", "37.85%", "27.88%", "32.35%"], "options_hi": ["29.11%", "37.85%", "27.88%", "32.35%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>C.P = Rs. 40, M.P = Rs. 50</p><p>Actual C.P = 40 * 850/1000</p><p>= Rs. 34</p><p>S.P = M.P * (100  -  Discount)/100 = 50 * 90/100 = Rs. 45</p><p>Profit = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>= (45  -  34) * 100/34</p><p>= 32.35%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P = Rs. 40, M.P = Rs. 50</p><p>Actual C.P = 40 * 850/1000</p><p>= Rs. 34</p><p>S.P = M.P * (100  -  Discount)/100 = 50 * 90/100 = Rs. 45</p><p>Profit = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>= (45  -  34) * 100/34</p><p>= 32.35%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of <img width=75 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24286/image007.png\">.</p>", "q_hi": "<p><img width=75 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24286/image007.png\"> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;.</p>", "options_en": ["38/33", "33/38", "16/99", "57/50"], "options_hi": ["38/33", "33/38", "16/99", "57/50"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=73 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24286/image008.png\"> </p><p>Let x = 0.4949...</p><p>100x = 49.4949..</p><p>100x  -  x = 49.4949.. - 0.4949..</p><p>99x = 49</p><p>x = 49/99</p><p>Similarly, </p><p>0.65.. = 65/99</p><p>=&gt; 49/99 + 65/99</p><p>=&gt; 114/99</p><p>=&gt; 38/33</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=73 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24286/image008.png\"> </p><p>Let x = 0.4949...</p><p>100x = 49.4949..</p><p>100x  -  x = 49.4949.. - 0.4949..</p><p>99x = 49</p><p>x = 49/99</p><p>Similarly, </p><p>0.65.. = 65/99</p><p>=&gt; 49/99 + 65/99</p><p>=&gt; 114/99</p><p>=&gt; 38/33</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat takes 1 hour 20 minutes to travel 64 km in upstream. If the speed of the stream is 12 km/h, then find the speed of boat in still water.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 64 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; 20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 12 km/h &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["60 km/h", "80 km/h", "75 km/h", "48 km/h"], "options_hi": ["60 km/h", "80 km/h", "75 km/h", "48 km/h"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of boat in still water = k</p><p>64/(k - 12) = 80/60</p><p>48 = (k - 12)</p><p>k = 60 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of boat in still water = k</p><p>64/(k - 12) = 80/60</p><p>48 = (k - 12)</p><p>k = 60 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length of a track is 1.4 km, the speeds of A and B are in the ratio of 7: 5 and A wins by 10 seconds. What is the approximate percentage of distance B covers when A finishes the race?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 1.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 7: 5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; A 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; A &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["80%", "65%", "90%", "71%"], "options_hi": ["80%", "65%", "90%", "71%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>A wins a 7 m race by 2 m.</p><p>So, in a 1.4 km race, A wins by 1400 x 2/7 = 400 m.</p><p>So, when A finishes the race, B covers = 1000 m</p><p>Required% = 1000 x 100/1400 = 71% (approximately.)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A wins a 7 m race by 2 m.</p><p>So, in a 1.4 km race, A wins by 1400 x 2/7 = 400 m.</p><p>So, when A finishes the race, B covers = 1000 m</p><p>Required% = 1000 x 100/1400 = 71% (approximately.)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (3x + 7) and (2x + 3) both are factors of px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q = 0, then</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (3x + 7) &#2324;&#2352; (2x + 3) &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379;</p>", "options_en": ["p = (3 + q)/4", "3p = q + 5", "3p = q  -  3", "2p = q"], "options_hi": ["p = (3 + q)/4", "3p = q + 5", "3p = q  -  3", "2p = q"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 7)(2x + 3) = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2</sup> + 14x + 9x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2 </sup>+ 23x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>Comparing both sides we get,</p><p>p = 6, q = 21</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 7)(2x + 3) = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2</sup> + 14x + 9x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2 </sup>+ 23x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>Comparing both sides we get,</p><p>p = 6, q = 21</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sides of a triangle are in the ratio 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 and its perimeter is 124 cm. What is the difference (in cm) between the largest and the smallest side?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 124 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["40 cm", "28 cm", "36 cm", "44 cm"], "options_hi": ["40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "44 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio = 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 </p><p>=&gt; 15 : 10 : 6</p><p>Difference between largest and smallest sides</p><p>=&gt; (15  -  6)/(15 + 10 + 6) * 124 = 36 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio = 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 </p><p>=&gt; 15 : 10 : 6</p><p>Difference between largest and smallest sides</p><p>=&gt; (15  -  6)/(15 + 10 + 6) * 124 = 36 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>For how many years, the number of female employees who were hired by the company is less than or equal to the average number of female employees who hired by the company in five years?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2351;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3", "2", "4", "5"], "options_hi": ["3", "2", "4", "5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Number of employees hired in 2012 = 8000 * 20/100 = 1600</p><p>Number of male employees hired in 2012 = 5400 * 72/360 = 1080</p><p>So, number of female employees hired in 2012 = 1600  -  1080 = 520 </p><p>Similarly, calculating the remaining data: </p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Total</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Male</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Female</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2012</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1600</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1080</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">520</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2013</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">960</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">675</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">285</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2014</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2240</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1620</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">620</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2015</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1200</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">900</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">300</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2016</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2000</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1125</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">875</td></tr></table><br><p>The average number of female employees who hired by the company in five years = (520 + 285 + 620 + 300 + 875)/5 = 520</p><p>For the years 2012, 2013, and 2015, number of female employees who were hired by the company is less than equal to the average number of female employees who were hired by the company in five years. </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of employees hired in 2012 = 8000 * 20/100 = 1600</p><p>Number of male employees hired in 2012 = 5400 * 72/360 = 1080</p><p>So, number of female employees hired in 2012 = 1600  -  1080 = 520 </p><p>Similarly, calculating the remaining data: </p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Total</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Male</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Female</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2012</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1600</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1080</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">520</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2013</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">960</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">675</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">285</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2014</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2240</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1620</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">620</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2015</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1200</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">900</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">300</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2016</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2000</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1125</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">875</td></tr></table><br><p>The average number of female employees who hired by the company in five years = (520 + 285 + 620 + 300 + 875)/5 = 520</p><p>For the years 2012, 2013, and 2015, number of female employees who were hired by the company is less than equal to the average number of female employees who were hired by the company in five years. </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is <b>not </b>irrational?</p><p>A = 18, B = 24, C = 36, D = 12</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2309;&#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2375;&#2351; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>A = 18, B = 24, C = 36, D = 12</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;(A + B + C + D)", "&radic;(A * B * C)", "&radic;(B * C * D)", "&radic;(A * B * D)"], "options_hi": ["&radic;(A + B + C + D)", "&radic;(A * B * C)", "&radic;(B * C * D)", "&radic;(A * B * D)"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>From 1: &radic;(A + B + C + D) = &radic;(18 + 24 + 36 + 12) = &radic;90 = 3&radic;10</p><p>From 2: &radic;(A * B * C) = &radic;(18 * 24 * 36) = 72&radic;3</p><p>From 3: &radic;(B * C * D) = &radic;(24 * 36 * 12) = 72&radic;2</p><p>From 4: &radic;(A * B * D) = &radic;(18 * 24 * 12) = 72 <b>(rational)</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From 1: &radic;(A + B + C + D) = &radic;(18 + 24 + 36 + 12) = &radic;90 = 3&radic;10</p><p>From 2: &radic;(A * B * C) = &radic;(18 * 24 * 36) = 72&radic;3</p><p>From 3: &radic;(B * C * D) = &radic;(24 * 36 * 12) = 72&radic;2</p><p>From 4: &radic;(A * B * D) = &radic;(18 * 24 * 12) = 72 <b>(rational)</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat running upstream takes 10 hours to cover a certain distance, while it takes 7 hours to cover the same distance running downstream. What is the ratio between the speed of the boat and that of the water current, respectively?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["17 : 5", "3 : 17", "2 : 17", "17 : 3"], "options_hi": ["17 : 5", "3 : 17", "2 : 17", "17 : 3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of upstream speed to downstream speed is inversely proportional to the ratio of time taken while travelling same distance upstream to downstream.</p><p>Ratio of upstream speed to downstream speed = 1/10: 1/7 = 7: 10</p><p>Ratio of speed of the boat to the water current = (10 + 7): (10  -  7)</p><p>= 17: 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of upstream speed to downstream speed is inversely proportional to the ratio of time taken while travelling same distance upstream to downstream.</p><p>Ratio of upstream speed to downstream speed = 1/10: 1/7 = 7: 10</p><p>Ratio of speed of the boat to the water current = (10 + 7): (10  -  7)</p><p>= 17: 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Solve the following expression :</p><p><div>&nbsp;80% of 520 - &radic;64 +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">18 x 5", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; :</p><p><div>&nbsp;80% of 520 - &radic;64 +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">18 x 5", "options_en": ["408", "438", "428", "418"], "options_hi": ["408", "438", "428", "418"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>80% of 520 - &radic;64 + (18 * 5)/3 = ?</p><p>416  -  8 + 30 = ?</p><p>? = 438</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>80% of 520 - &radic;64 + (18 * 5)/3 = ?</p><p>416  -  8 + 30 = ?</p><p>? = 438</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "options_en": ["(a - b) (b  -  c) = 2", "(a  -  b) (a  -  c) = 1", "(b  -  c) (c  -  a) = 2", "(a  -  b) (b  -  c) = 1"], "options_hi": ["(a - b) (b - c) = 2", "(a - b) (a - c) = 1", "(b - c) (c - a) = 2", "(a - b) (b - c) = 1"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=307 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image020.png\"></p><p><img width=153 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=153 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=111 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image023.png\"></p><p><img width=109 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image024.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=307 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image020.png\"></p><p><img width=153 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=153 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=111 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image023.png\"></p><p><img width=109 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18409/image024.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Express 0.32<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">64", "q_hi": "<p>0.32<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">64", "options_en": ["816/2475", "812/2475", "808/2475", "820/2475"], "options_hi": ["816/2475", "812/2475", "808/2475", "820/2475"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>23/31 = 0.74</p><p>(a) 27/39 = 0.69</p><p>(b) 15/28 = 0.53</p><p>(c) 22/29 = 0.758 [Nearest]</p><p>(d) 17/22 = 0.77</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>23/31 = 0.74</p><p>(a) 27/39 = 0.69</p><p>(b) 15/28 = 0.53</p><p>(c) 22/29 = 0.758 [Nearest]</p><p>(d) 17/22 = 0.77</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of a parallelogram with base 26 cm and height 18 cm is:</p>", "q_hi": "26 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:", "options_en": ["234 cm<sup>2</sup>", "936 cm<sup>2</sup>", "932 cm<sup>2</sup>", "468 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["234 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "936 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "932 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "468 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Base=26 cm</p><p>Height= 18 cm</p><p>Area of parallelogram= base*height</p><p>Area=26*18 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>=468 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Base=26 cm</p><p>Height= 18 cm</p><p>Area of parallelogram= base*height</p><p>Area=26*18 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>=468 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three persons A, B and C start running around a circular stadium and complete a single round in 5 sec, (X  -  3) sec and (X  -  1) sec respectively. After 315 sec, they meet again at the starting point for the first time. Find the time taken by B to complete a single round of stadium.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;, (X - 3) &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2324;&#2352; (X - 1) &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 315 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2357;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7 sec", "11 sec", "9 sec", "13 sec"], "options_hi": ["7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>We know that the time at which they met again is equal to the LCM of 5, (X  -  3) and (X  -  1).</p><p>SO,</p><p>5* (X  -  3)* (X  -  1) = 315</p><p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  4X + 3 = 63</p><p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  4X  -  60 = 0</p><p>X<sup>2 </sup> -  10X + 6X  -  60 = 0</p><p>(X  -  10) (X + 6) = 0</p><p>X = 10 or -6</p><p>X = -6 is not possible.</p><p>SO, X = 10</p><p>Therefore, time taken by B to complete one single round of stadium = (10  -  3) = 7 sec.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that the time at which they met again is equal to the LCM of 5, (X  -  3) and (X  -  1).</p><p>SO,</p><p>5* (X  -  3)* (X  -  1) = 315</p><p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  4X + 3 = 63</p><p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  4X  -  60 = 0</p><p>X<sup>2 </sup> -  10X + 6X  -  60 = 0</p><p>(X  -  10) (X + 6) = 0</p><p>X = 10 or -6</p><p>X = -6 is not possible.</p><p>SO, X = 10</p><p>Therefore, time taken by B to complete one single round of stadium = (10  -  3) = 7 sec.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The graph of two linear equations 3x + 5y = 7 and 9x + 15y = 21 will be -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2376;&#2326;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; 3x + 5y = 7 &#2324;&#2352; 9x + 15y = 21 &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; -</p>", "options_en": ["coincident", "Parallel", "Intersecting at one point", "Intersecting at two points"], "options_hi": ["&#2350;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2348;", "&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;", "&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;", "&#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>3x + 5y = 7 and 9x + 15y = 21</p><p>a<sub>1</sub> = 3, b<sub>1</sub> = 5, c<sub>1</sub> = 7,</p><p>a<sub>2</sub> = 9 b<sub>2</sub> = 15, c<sub>2</sub> = 21</p><p>a<sub>1</sub>/a<sub>2</sub> = 3/9 = 1/3</p><p>b<sub>1</sub>/b<sub>2</sub> = 5/15 = 1/3</p><p>c<sub>1</sub>/c<sub>2</sub> = 7/21 = 1/3</p><p>Since, a<sub>1</sub>/a<sub>2</sub> = b<sub>1</sub>/b<sub>2</sub> = c<sub>1</sub>/c<sub>2</sub></p><p>So, these are coincident lines.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3x + 5y = 7 and 9x + 15y = 21</p><p>a<sub>1</sub> = 3, b<sub>1</sub> = 5, c<sub>1</sub> = 7,</p><p>a<sub>2</sub> = 9 b<sub>2</sub> = 15, c<sub>2</sub> = 21</p><p>a<sub>1</sub>/a<sub>2</sub> = 3/9 = 1/3</p><p>b<sub>1</sub>/b<sub>2</sub> = 5/15 = 1/3</p><p>c<sub>1</sub>/c<sub>2</sub> = 7/21 = 1/3</p><p>Since, a<sub>1</sub>/a<sub>2</sub> = b<sub>1</sub>/b<sub>2</sub> = c<sub>1</sub>/c<sub>2</sub></p><p>So, these are coincident lines.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If number of terms are equal in both the series given below, then find the last term of the series B.</p><p>Series A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>Series B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2346;&#2342; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p>", "options_en": ["371", "350", "329", "308"], "options_hi": ["371", "350", "329", "308"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>For series A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>The following series is in the arithmetic progression, as the difference between every two consecutive terms is same. So,</p><p>a = 126, d = 139  -  126 = 13</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= 321</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>321 = 126 + (n  -  1) x 13</p><p>n = 16</p><p>Now, for series B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p><p>a = 56, d = 77  -  56 = 21</p><p>n = 16</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>= 56 + 15 x 21</p><p>= 371</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For series A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>The following series is in the arithmetic progression, as the difference between every two consecutive terms is same. So,</p><p>a = 126, d = 139  -  126 = 13</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= 321</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>321 = 126 + (n  -  1) x 13</p><p>n = 16</p><p>Now, for series B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p><p>a = 56, d = 77  -  56 = 21</p><p>n = 16</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>= 56 + 15 x 21</p><p>= 371</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a test consisting of 75 questions carrying one mark each, Samir answered 75% of the first 40 questions correctly. What approximate percent of the other 35 questions does he need to answer correctly to score 80% in the entire test?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; 75 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 40 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 75% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 80% &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; 35 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["90", "75", "86", "60"], "options_hi": ["90", "75", "86", "60"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total questions he need to answer correctly = 75 x 0.8 = 60</p><p>He answers 0.75x40 = 30 correct out of first 40.</p><p>So he must answer 30 correct out of the remaining 35</p><p>Required % = 30/35 x 100 = 85.71% = 86%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total questions he need to answer correctly = 75 x 0.8 = 60</p><p>He answers 0.75x40 = 30 correct out of first 40.</p><p>So he must answer 30 correct out of the remaining 35</p><p>Required % = 30/35 x 100 = 85.71% = 86%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A = 1/(4+&radic;7) &amp; B = 1/(3-&radic;7), find the value of 27A + 6B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 1/(4+&radic;7) &#2324;&#2352; B = 1/(3-&radic;7) &#2361;&#2376;, 27A + 6B &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["18", "33", "21", "27"], "options_hi": ["18", "33", "21", "27"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>A = 1/(4+&radic;7) = 1/(4+&radic;7) x (4-&radic;7)/(4-&radic;7) = (4 - &radic;7)/(16 - 7) = (4 - &radic;7)/9</p> <p>27A = 12  -  3&radic;7</p> <p>A = 1/(3-&radic;7) = 1/(3-&radic;7) x (3+&radic;7)/(3+&radic;7) = (3+&radic;7)/9-7 = (3+&radic;7)/2</p> <p>6B = 9 + 3&radic;7</p> <p>27A + 6B = 12  -  3&radic;7 + 9 + 3&radic;7 = 21</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A = 1/(4+&radic;7) = 1/(4+&radic;7) x (4-&radic;7)/(4-&radic;7) = (4 - &radic;7)/(16 - 7) = (4 - &radic;7)/9</p> <p>27A = 12  -  3&radic;7</p> <p>A = 1/(3-&radic;7) = 1/(3-&radic;7) x (3+&radic;7)/(3+&radic;7) = (3+&radic;7)/9-7 = (3+&radic;7)/2</p> <p>6B = 9 + 3&radic;7</p> <p>27A + 6B = 12  -  3&radic;7 + 9 + 3&radic;7 = 21</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}]}